                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "db7c8ba3-d785-3bb4-8edb-be3b0b57fa4b",
                                        "entry_id": "a615fc8b-48a9-3490-a4e3-4074a78aa8ac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Kreuzungspunkt von zwei Autobahnen auf unterschiedlichen Ebenen, wobei die beiden Autobahnen durch Ein- und Ausfahrten und Verbindungsrampen miteinander verbunden sind"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Straßenverkehr"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ef87112-ba84-4752-81ca-a4ee7f94bdf9",
                                                "sense_id": "db7c8ba3-d785-3bb4-8edb-be3b0b57fa4b",
                                                "text": "Das Autobahnkreuz Stuttgart wird täglich von etwa 215.000 Fahrzeugen befahren."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "71052d7d-7031-42c6-a677-65a29706e7e0",
                        "source_entry_id": "675f01cd-0db4-336d-a060-9bb61327804b",
                        "source_sense_id": "9c3db31a-a953-34e7-ae3c-e8529cfcdb55",
                        "source_sense_description": "échangeur autoroutier",
                        "target_lang_word": "interchange",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "interchange",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a2a86d00-95bf-340a-88c5-eb7c25aaad9f",
                                        "entry_id": "282f6a88-8368-386a-b987-58d372d91f40",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "to switch (each of two things)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "377fb7d6-1688-410a-a149-dd0278f98937",
                                                "sense_id": "a2a86d00-95bf-340a-88c5-eb7c25aaad9f",
                                                "text": "to interchange places"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "62a9f0fe-e933-3f76-8711-5e030c7a79c1",
                                        "entry_id": "282f6a88-8368-386a-b987-58d372d91f40",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "to mutually give and receive (something); to exchange"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b6903b7-5d11-42d6-b347-293f99705014",
                                                "sense_id": "62a9f0fe-e933-3f76-8711-5e030c7a79c1",
                                                "text": "I shall interchange / My waned state for Henry's regal crown."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4fac57ae-2bf8-3217-8b9d-8e86109045d4",
                                        "entry_id": "282f6a88-8368-386a-b987-58d372d91f40",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "to swap or change places"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "24f02e60-73c8-44ed-8c7e-a91e3fc536c2",
                                                "sense_id": "4fac57ae-2bf8-3217-8b9d-8e86109045d4",
                                                "text": "The poem is written in an alef-lamed, bet-nun acrostic form. This is a formula of permutation of letters wherein the first interchanges with the twelfth, the second with the thirteenth, etc."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b1928b37-18a9-3ac4-99a3-957307525cc3",
                                        "entry_id": "282f6a88-8368-386a-b987-58d372d91f40",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "to alternate; to intermingle or vary"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e3a74f3c-158b-4ace-9412-8cb5312e6f44",
                                                "sense_id": "b1928b37-18a9-3ac4-99a3-957307525cc3",
                                                "text": "to interchange cares with pleasures"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "63916657-f8f5-35e1-a599-7ea08359e30e",
                                        "entry_id": "282f6a88-8368-386a-b987-58d372d91f40",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To act as or carry out an interchange (noun, senses 2, 3)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b17b446d-2de5-4a72-b369-8d19be24aa7f",
                                                "sense_id": "63916657-f8f5-35e1-a599-7ea08359e30e",
                                                "text": "But those 13 miles go through central London, and where the Underground interchanges with Crossrail, its own stations will be boosted and glamorised, especially at Bond Street and Tottenham Court Road."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd093af1-6683-4e8d-a9ff-86ef7c515b1a",
                                                "sense_id": "63916657-f8f5-35e1-a599-7ea08359e30e",
                                                "text": "The expectation is that about one-third of passengers will choose to interchange at Old Oak, while two-thirds will prefer to travel on to Euston."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "interchange",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1b8274b4-68e5-32c0-b345-ef33685c0099",
                                        "entry_id": "5800b1fb-4f2a-3af4-a323-eca833c0661a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An act of interchanging."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "797c615f-ad1a-4db7-97d9-6f73bcd96820",
                                                "sense_id": "1b8274b4-68e5-32c0-b345-ef33685c0099",
                                                "text": "That was one of three superb saves Hennessey made in the opening 45 minutes, the best of which was from Dzeko, who had been released by a slick interchange involving Silva and Sergio Aguero."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d730cee9-c5b3-3527-8ef0-606090068409",
                                        "entry_id": "5800b1fb-4f2a-3af4-a323-eca833c0661a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A highway junction in which traffic may change from one road to another without crossing a stream of traffic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0256c386-6b61-3de4-8989-d6d5cec72f6a",
                                        "entry_id": "5800b1fb-4f2a-3af4-a323-eca833c0661a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A junction in which traffic may merge to enter or diverge to exit a limited-access highway to access a surface street, without crossing traffic on the main highway."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "79c0abee-f9af-3685-b20c-a2d3ae3e2eb6",
                                        "entry_id": "5800b1fb-4f2a-3af4-a323-eca833c0661a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A connection between two or more lines, services or modes of transport; a station at which such a connection can be made."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "43dd6e07-9e7e-4e2d-86ed-276e12bc98d1",
                                                "sense_id": "79c0abee-f9af-3685-b20c-a2d3ae3e2eb6",
                                                "text": "Holborn tube station is the only interchange between the London Underground Central and Piccadilly Lines."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e23b617-99ea-4a86-84e5-36345b99638f",
                                                "sense_id": "79c0abee-f9af-3685-b20c-a2d3ae3e2eb6",
                                                "text": "Moving on again, I catch another GWR Class 802 bound for Oxford via the Cotswold Line. Our first stop is at one of the newest stations on the network - Worcestershire Parkway, which opened on February 23. It's a four-platform (actually three-platform) split-level interchange with the line from Birmingham to Bristol."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c3cf232d-7cfc-366e-b740-05fb067bb3e0",
                                        "entry_id": "5800b1fb-4f2a-3af4-a323-eca833c0661a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A back-and-forth interaction; an exchange."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f2192c8-9707-49c5-9ea9-0b176d76b355",
                                                "sense_id": "c3cf232d-7cfc-366e-b740-05fb067bb3e0",
                                                "text": "David and I were not \"intimate\" friends. There was always a certain old-worldly formality about our interchanges. There was something professorial and distant about David, something that commanded respect, partially, I think, because he was so respectful himself."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
